0..71 Comment "// A row may name an instance of an interface by a label (#2271): `say`"
72..136 Comment "// performs `Console` through its instance `out`, apart from the"
137..211 Comment "// interface\'s default and from every other instance, so one row holds two"
212..280 Comment "// instances of one interface. The label is a parameter the function"
281..356 Comment "// abstracts, placed after every parameter it writes: a call supplies it by"
357..431 Comment "// name, `say[.out = c]()`, or omits it and passes the one instance of the"
432..507 Comment "// interface handled where the call stands, a capability scope\'s capability"
508..574 Comment "// or a label of the caller\'s own row (Brachthäuser, Schuster and"
575..646 Comment "// Ostermann, \"Effects as Capabilities: Effect Handlers and Lightweight"
647..704 Comment "// Effect Polymorphism\", OOPSLA 2020). What refuses is in"
705..759 Comment "// `../../pathological/control/named-instances.gandr`."
761..832 Comment "/// A line printed through the instance `out`, the capability its label"
833..843 Comment "/// binds."
